    "chunk_index": 1,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "8a3a6a64fdee7d2024eeca5ed576f3a6",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 840,
    "chunk_text": "The Prime Minister acknowledged that while the university system has expanded over the years, quality has not kept pace. She pointed to gaps in foundational learning at the school level that are creating pressure on the higher education sector.\n\nShe noted that upcoming education reforms aim to address these systemic issues and better prepare students for university and beyond. \u201cThrough the new education reform, we are working to change this situation.\u201d\n\nDr. Amarasuriya reiterated the Government\u2019s commitment to academic freedom while drawing a line at harmful conduct. \u201cAt the same time, we place no restrictions on university students raising their voices, protesting, or engaging in student politics to claim their rights.\u201d\n\nShe concluded by reaffirming the Government\u2019s policy to ensure access to high-quality education."
  },
