    "chunk_size_bytes": 1926,
    "chunk_text": "Dialog Enhances 5G Roaming, Now Covering 70 Countries and 150 Global Mobile Operators\n\nDialog Axiata PLC, Sri Lanka\u2019s #1 connectivity provider, has expanded its 5G roaming footprint to 70 countries in collaboration with 150 global mobile operators \u2013 reinforcing its commitment to delivering seamless mobile connectivity and high-speed data access for Sri Lankan travellers, whether flying for business or leisure.\n\nBuilding on its 2023 milestone of enabling 5G roaming across 50+ countries with 100+ mobile operators, Dialog continues to extend its global reach. With support for speeds of up to 1 Gbps, the expanded network ensures that customers with 5G-compatible devices enjoy fast, reliable connectivity wherever they travel \u2013 reflecting Dialog\u2019s ongoing efforts to innovate and lead in telecommunications.\n\nThis development builds upon Dialog\u2019s leadership in South Asia\u2019s 5G landscape, which began in 2018 with the first demonstration of 5G capabilities in the region. Today, Dialog\u2019s 5G roaming network stands among the most extensive in the region, delivering an enhanced experience for customers on the move.\n\n\u201cAt Dialog, we are proud to extend our 5G roaming services to 70 countries and 150 mobile operators globally, further solidifying our position as a leader in technological innovation,\u201d said Lim Li San, Group Chief Operating Officer of Dialog Axiata PLC. \u201cOur commitment to providing seamless, high-speed connectivity for our customers remains unwavering, and this milestone underscores our mission to deliver a world-class mobile experience, whether at home or abroad.\u201d\n\nDialog remains dedicated to enhancing the mobile experience by expanding its 5G roaming footprint and ensuring the best in global connectivity and performance. For more information on roaming, visit https://www.dialog.lk/roaming/4g-5g-country-list.\n\nBank of Ceylon crowned Sri Lanka\u2019s Most Valuable Brand in 2025"
