  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-08-04-islandlk-7a9109d5",
    "num": "islandlk-7a9109d5",
    "date_str": "2025-08-04",
    "description": "PC polls, false dilemma and hypocrisy",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/pc-polls-false-dilemma-and-hypocrisy/",
    "lang": "en",
    "newspaper_id": "islandlk",
    "time_ut": 1754329680.0,
    "chunk_id": "2025-08-04-islandlk-7a9109d5-0000",
    "chunk_index": 0,
    "language": "en",
    "md5": "ff837dd182057d89ecbf3f0c28755143",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1833,
    "chunk_text": "PC polls, false dilemma and hypocrisy\n\nThe SJB-led Opposition is given to selective amnesia, just like the NPP government, which has conveniently forgotten most of its election pledges. It turns a blind eye to the issues that are politically disadvantageous to it and takes up the ones it can flog to gain some political mileage. It has suddenly become concerned about devolution and remembered that the Provincial Council (PC) elections are long overdue!\n\nAddressing the media, SJB MP Dayasiri Jayasekera yesterday called upon the government either to hold the PC polls or to scrap the PC system. This is a classic example of a false dilemma/dichotomy, as logicians may say. The Opposition\u2019s call in question obviously has not stemmed from any concern for devolution or the people\u2019s franchise. The SJB and like-minded others seem to think that the government, struggling on several fronts, is not ready for another election. They are acting out of expediency rather than principle.\n\nThe SJB is of the view that a minor amendment to the Provincial Council Elections Act will help clear obstacles to conducting the PC elections under the Proportional Representation (PR) system. The SJB seniors themselves are responsible for the unholy mess the PC system is in; the PCs have been without elected representatives for about eight years. The country has had four Presidents and three governments since the PC polls were postponed in 2017!\n\nThere is no gainsaying that the PC polls should be held without further delay since no election should be postponed for political reasons. Parliament should pass an amendment to the PC Elections Act immediately to provide for conducting the PC polls under the PR system. Whether the PC system has become a white elephant and should be scrapped is an issue that should be addressed separately."
  },
  {
    "doc_type": "lk_news",
    "doc_id": "2025-08-04-islandlk-7a9109d5",
    "num": "islandlk-7a9109d5",
    "date_str": "2025-08-04",
    "description": "PC polls, false dilemma and hypocrisy",
    "url_metadata": "http://island.lk/pc-polls-false-dilemma-and-hypocrisy/",
