    "language": "en",
    "md5": "a4bbbb14af37a8eb295f9168c3a75fa1",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1718,
    "chunk_text": "There is no gainsaying that the PC polls should be held without further delay since no election should be postponed for political reasons. Parliament should pass an amendment to the PC Elections Act immediately to provide for conducting the PC polls under the PR system. Whether the PC system has become a white elephant and should be scrapped is an issue that should be addressed separately.\n\nThis newspaper was among those who vehemently condemned the deplorable manner in which that amendment bill which was made out to be a move to guarantee a 30% quota for women was stuffed, at the committee stage, with sections changing the electoral system to delay the PC polls. What was passed by Parliament was vastly different from the bill examined by the Supreme Court.\n\nThe vociferous SJB MPs who are calling upon the incumbent government to hold the PC polls were in the Yahapalana government. Nothing can be done about bad laws passed by Parliament in this country because there is no constitutional provision for the post-enactment judicial review of legislation. The need for a constitutional amendment to provide for judicial scrutiny of all laws after their passage cannot be overstated.\n\nThe SBJ MPs, who are now on a campaign to pressure the government to hold the PC polls immediately, have demonstrated their hypocrisy. However, it is incumbent upon the government and the Opposition to amend the PC Elections Act in a transparent manner, expeditiously, enabling the Election Commission to hold the delayed PC polls.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
