    "chunk_text": "Cabinet grants \u2018approved Enterprise\u2019 status to four import companies for re-export of selected spices\n\nApproval was granted at the cabinet meeting held on 18-12-2023 for the procedure to import and process the selected spices to reexport in the form of oil extract, oleoresin, and residue.\n\nImport and export regulations No. 10 of 2024 have been imposed for that purpose. According to the aforementioned\n\nregulations, several enterprises have already signed supplementary agreements with the Board of Investment of Sri Lanka to import and process selected spices. The Board of Investment of Sri Lanka has recommended the granting of \u201capproved enterprise\u201d status to these below mentioned enterprises.\n\nAccordingly, the Cabinet of Ministers has agreed to the proposal presented by the President, in his capacity as the Minister of Finance, Planning, and Economic Development, to grant\n\n\u201capproved enterprise\u201d status to the following enterprises that have fulfilled the requirements of the approved procedure for re-exporting selected spices in the form of oil extract, oleoresin, and residue.\n\nDelimitation committee appointed to review the recommendations of the delimitation committee of the years 2012 and 2021\n\nDeclaration of Government Financial Performance for the second quarter of the year 2025 presented to Cabinet\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
