    "chunk_text": "The policy paper reveals that Sri Lanka had previously enjoyed a trade surplus with the U.S., with Sri Lankan exports reaching USD 3.37 billion, compared to USD 738 million in imports. However, exports have now slumped:\n\nRubber product exports, including tyres (USD 12.5 million worth), are also expected to be affected.\n\nOverall U.S. exports to Sri Lanka have fallen by 11% year-on-year, with imports from Sri Lanka plummeting 26.1%.\n\nTennakoon warned that these shifts are not isolated incidents, but part of a broader pattern of economic uncertainty and instability engineered through fluctuating American policies:\n\n\u201cThe Trump tariff regime is not just a trade mechanism. It is a tool of economic influence. The instability it creates is a deliberate strategy, he cautioned.\n\nSLT-MOBITEL achieves double recognition at National Business Excellence Awards 2025\n\nComBank\u2019s Rs. 15 billion Green Bond issue oversubscribed on opening day\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
