    "chunk_size_bytes": 1830,
    "chunk_text": "Skin, body and hair \u2026\n\nAll of us, especially the ladies, would love to take care of our skin, body, and hair.\n\nThis week, my Beauty Tips revolve around items that you already have in your kitchen cupboard.\n\nYou will need 01 teaspoon of turmeric, 01 teaspoon of organic honey, and 01 tablespoon of natural yoghurt.\n\nMix all the ingredients together thoroughly in a bowl and then apply the mixture to freshly washed, dry skin. Leave the mask on for 20 minutes, and then rinse with warm water and follow with your usual skincare routine.\n\nYou will need 01 avocado, 01 tablespoon of honey (optional), and 02 tablespoons of coconut or olive oil.\n\nMix all the ingredients in a blender to get a smooth consistency that feels like a conditioner. (If you don\u2019t have a blender, mash up the avocado with a fork and whip in the other ingredients for a lightweight texture.) Apply the mask all over dry hair, focusing on your ends and also applying to your scalp. Leave the mask on for one hour, and then wash your hair with shampoo and conditioner, as usual.\n\nOn clean skin, take one slice of your orange and gently rub it on your skin. If you\u2019re using orange juice, then apply a little to a cotton pad and sweep it across your face, like you\u2019re using toner. Keep the juice on your face for 10 minutes while you enjoy a glass of juice or your orange \u2013 got to get those vitamins inside for glowing skin and a good immune boost \u2013 then rinse your face with water and apply any serums and moisturisers.\n\nCrack 01 large egg in a bowl and separate the yolk so only the egg white remains. Whisk the mixture, using a fork, until it thickens slightly. Apply the mixture to cleansed skin then wash it off once it dries (around 15 minutes) with lukewarm water.\n\nYou will need 01 green tea bag and 01 teaspoon of sweet almond oil or Vaseline."
