    "md5": "29b0756d79c8f7c6f24773d638ee9ffd",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1713,
    "chunk_text": "Tara Rajapaksha recognised as Best Korean Language Teacher at Asia Miracle Awards 2025\n\nTara Rajapaksha, founder of the Korean Language Centre (KLC) in Kadawatha, has been recognized as the\u00a0Best Korean Language Teacher of the Year\u00a0at the prestigious\u00a0Asia Miracle Awards 2025. The award ceremony took place recently at the\u00a0Taj Samudra Hotel\u00a0in Colombo, celebrating her outstanding contributions to language education and workforce development.\n\nWith over\u00a025 years of teaching experience, Rajapaksha has played a pivotal role in empowering Sri Lankan youth by equipping them with Korean language skills essential for employment opportunities in South Korea. Her institution,\u00a0KLC Kadawatha, has trained thousands of students for the\u00a0Korean Language Proficiency Exam (EPS-TOPIK), with many achieving high scores and securing jobs in key industries such as\u00a0manufacturing, construction, shipping, and fisheries.\n\nKLC stands out for its\u00a0personalized teaching approach, ensuring each student receives individual attention to build confidence and proficiency.\n\nUnder a\u00a0government-to-government agreement, Sri Lanka receives an annual quota of employment opportunities in South Korea, facilitated by the\u00a0Sri Lanka Bureau of Foreign Employment (SLBFE). Unskilled workers aged\u00a018\u201339\u00a0who pass the\u00a0EPS-TOPIK exam\u00a0can secure jobs with a\u00a0minimum monthly salary of LKR 500,000\u00a0in sectors like\u00a0manufacturing, construction, agriculture, and fisheries.\n\nAminda Perera assumes duties as Chairman of SANASA Life Insurance\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
