    "chunk_text": "The Colombo Stock Exchange (CSE), in collaboration with the Securities and Exchange Commission of Sri Lanka (SEC) and the stock broking industry, will be hosting the \u2018Invest Sri Lanka\u2019 Investor Forum in Singapore on August 12.\n\nThe event can be viewed live from 6.30 am (GMT +5:30) via the following link:\n\nSri Lanka\u2019s Almas increases share in Galle Face Capital Partners to over 10-pct\n\nElsewhere, Tokyo stocks ended higher boosted by positive earnings reports in the fiscal first quarter, Japan\u2019s The Mainichi newspaper said on Friday. The Nikkei 225 Index moved 1.85 percent higher, or 761.33 points from Thursday, to 41,820.48.\n\nThe Pakistan Stock Exchange\u2019s KSE 100 Index rose on buying in key sectors including automobile assemblers, commercial banks, oil and gas exploration companies and refinery, Pakistan\u2019s Business Recorder newspaper said. The index last traded 0.88 percent higher at 146,657.58.\n\nMeanwhile India\u2019s Nifty 50 rose 0.91 percent to 24,585.05, while the BSE Sensex was 0.93 percent higher at 80,604.08.\n\nAs at 3.40 pm Sri Lankan time, spot gold was trading at 3,370.31 US dollars, down 35.64 US dollars. (Colombo/Aug11/2025)"
