    "md5": "d15851682b6461d5992717f1f7a57f2b",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1488,
    "chunk_text": "Dialog sustains growth momentum, delivering strong 1H 2025 performance\n\nDialog Axiata PLC announced its consolidated financial results for the six months ended 30th June 2025. Financial results included those of Dialog Axiata PLC (the \u201cCompany\u201d) and of Dialog Axiata Group (the \u201cGroup\u201d).\n\nThe Group delivered robust results across its Mobile, Fixed Line, Digital Pay Television, and Tele-infrastructure businesses, achieving 6% year-to-date (\u201cYTD\u201d) revenue growth to Rs87.4Bn in 1H 2025. This was despite the strategic scaling down of low-margin international wholesale business, amounting to approximately Rs10Bn. On a quarter-on-quarter (\u201cQoQ\u201d) basis, revenue increased 2% to Rs44.1Bn, driven primarily by data revenue expansion. Core revenue for the period reached Rs84.2Bn, up 21% YTD.\n\nGroup Earnings Before Interest, Tax, Depreciation and Amortisation (\u201cEBITDA\u201d) recorded a growth of 50% YTD to Rs40.5Bn in 1H 2025, with QoQ EBITDA rising 5% to Rs20.8Bn. The strong performance reflects both revenue growth and operational efficiencies. The EBITDA margin improved by 13.5 percentage points compared to 1H 2024, reaching 46.3%, surpassing pre-crisis margin.\n\nGroup Net Profit After Tax (\u201cNPAT\u201d) was recorded at Rs9.2Bn in 1H 2025, more than doubling YTD. QoQ NPAT grew by 23% to Rs5.1Bn, supported by improved EBITDA and lower finance costs. In line with improved operational performance, Operating Free Cash Flow (\u201cOFCF\u201d) improved by 78% YTD to Rs22.1Bn."
  },
