    "chunk_size_bytes": 1583,
    "chunk_text": "Group Net Profit After Tax (\u201cNPAT\u201d) was recorded at Rs9.2Bn in 1H 2025, more than doubling YTD. QoQ NPAT grew by 23% to Rs5.1Bn, supported by improved EBITDA and lower finance costs. In line with improved operational performance, Operating Free Cash Flow (\u201cOFCF\u201d) improved by 78% YTD to Rs22.1Bn.\n\nDialog Television (\u201cDTV\u201d) consolidated its leadership position in the Digital Pay Television market, maintaining a subscriber base of over 1.6Mn as of end 1H 2025. DTV revenue reached Rs6.4Bn for 1H 2025 and Rs3.3Bn for Q2 2025, up 5% YTD and 5% QoQ. Growth was supported by higher Subscription and Advertising revenues. DTV EBITDA grew 24% YTD to Rs1.2Bn for 1H 2025; however, NPAT was recorded at a negative Rs479Mn for the period.\n\nDialog Broadband Networks (\u201cDBN\u201d), encompassing the Group\u2019s Fixed Telecommunications, Broadband, and International Businesses, posted revenue of Rs17.4Bn for 1H 2025 and Rs8.4Bn for Q2 2025, down 38% YTD and 8% QoQ. This decline was primarily due to the scaling down of low-margin international wholesale operations. Nevertheless, DBN EBITDA increased 20% YTD to Rs9.6Bn in 1H 2025, driven by growth in Broadband business. NPAT recorded a growth of 67% YTD to Rs2.8Bn.\n\nCT Holdings and Cargills come to the fore of CSE trading in the wake of profit-takings\n\nCEAT ranks as Sri Lanka\u2019s Most Valuable Tyre Brand in 2025 Brand Finance Report\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
