    "chunk_size_bytes": 1257,
    "chunk_text": "Addressing the gathering, Speaker Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne highlighted the longstanding relationship between Sri Lanka and Pakistan and noted that cooperation between the two countries extends across trade, education, defence, and people-to-people ties. He expressed gratitude for Pakistan\u2019s continued support to Sri Lanka and emphasised that the revival of the Friendship Association marks an important step towards strengthening this partnership.\n\nIn his remarks, Minister Anura Karunathilaka thanked the members for electing him and stated that the Association would provide a meaningful platform for dialogue, cooperation, and trust-building between the two nations. He also invited all members of the Association to actively contribute to its activities.\n\nDelivering the vote of thanks, Farook extended his gratitude to the Speaker, the High Commissioner, and all members present. He acknowledged Pakistan\u2019s continued support to Sri Lanka and expressed his commitment to work with fellow members to achieve the objectives of the Association.\n\nPrior to this meeting, the Pakistani High Commissioner met with the Speaker to discuss strengthening bilateral relations, with a focus on enhancing cooperation in investment, trade, tourism, and education."
