    "chunk_size_bytes": 1337,
    "chunk_text": "Of that no-faith battle\n\nThe Opposition has handed over its no-faith motion against Deputy Minister of Defence Maj. Gen. (retd.) Aruna Jayasekera to Speaker Dr. Jagath Wickramaratne. It insists that Jayasekera, as the Security Forces Commander of the Eastern Province in 2019, failed to prevent the Easter Sunday terrorist bombings carried out by the National Thowheed Jamaath (NTJ), which was based in the East, and therefore it is not possible to conduct an impartial probe into the terror attacks while he is functioning as the Deputy Minister of Defence.\n\nThe JVP-led NPP has a two-thirds majority in Parliament, and therefore the no-faith motion against Jayasekera has no chance of passage. However, the Opposition will be able to make the government either defend Jayasekera or ask him to resign as the Deputy Minister of Defence. The SJB and its allies have built a strong case against Jayasekera, and it will be a huge political gamble for the government to throw its weight behind him. The Catholic Church has also expressed serious concern about his holding the post of Deputy Defence Minister during investigations into the Easter Sunday terror attacks. So, the government finds itself in a dilemma. It cannot throw Jayasekera to the wolves by asking him to resign, for such action will amount to a victory for the Opposition."
  },
