    "chunk_size_bytes": 1847,
    "chunk_text": "Sri Lanka\u2019s Hatton National Bank net up 37-pct in June quarter\n\nECONOMYNEXT \u2013 Profits at Sri Lanka\u2019s Hatton National Bank, which also has an insurance unit, grew 37 percent from a year ago to 11.74 billion rupees, helped by loan loss reversals and depreciation gains, despite a fall in net interest income, interim accounts show.\n\nHNB group reported earnings of 20.54 rupees for the quarter. In the six months to June HNB reported earnings of 39.25 rupees on total profits of 22.4 billion rupees, which grew 42 percent.\n\nNet fee income and commission income grew 20 percent to 5.7 billion rupees with card use and digital transactions contributing, the bank said.\n\nRupee depreciation had helped boost forex income to 2.8 billion rupees in the half year.\n\nAt standalone bank level, net interest income fell 8 percent to 50.1 billion rupees in the June quarter with interest income falling 8 percent to 50.1 billion rupees and interest expenses also falling 8 percent to 28.2 billion rupees.\n\nLoans grew 12 percent to 1,186 billion rupees from December to June, debt instruments rose 12 percent to 828 billion rupees.\n\nUp to March loans had grown to 1,078 billion rupees and debt securities to 755 billion rupees.\n\nThere was a 4.6 billion rupee reversal of loan loss provisions, compared to an 814 million rupee provision last year, helping boost profits.\n\nImpaired Stage 3 loan loss ratio was 1.82 percent, down from 1.88 percent, amid loan growth and provision reversals.\n\nDeposits grew 9 percent to 1,864 billion rupees. Up to March deposits were 1,723 billion rupees.\n\nHNB gross assets at bank level grew 9 percent to 2,267 billion rupees from December.\n\nTier 1 capital was 18.42 percent, down from 19.59 percent. Total capital adequacy was 22.46 percent, down from 23.9 percent, higher than the required 13.5 percent. (Colombo/Aug13/2025)"
