    "chunk_size_bytes": 1318,
    "chunk_text": "Crime and politics\n\nNewly appointed IGP Priyantha Weerasooriya has promised to crack down on the netherworld of crime and drugs. He made this pledge at a media briefing, after assuming duties in his new position, where he had been acting previously. Stressing the need for new laws to combat crime effectively and expressing the hope that the NPP government would make them soon, he identified a nexus between criminals and politicians who had been in power previously as one of the key factors that had facilitated the rise of the underworld. Thankfully, the situation had changed under the new dispensation, but some criminals continued to maintain contacts with their former political bosses, he said, promising to bring back all the Sri Lankan underworld kingpins hiding overseas and make them face the full force of the law.\n\nOne cannot but agree with the new police chief. It however needs to be added that the sorry state of affairs in the Police Department is also due to the subservience of some of its officers and men to politicians. Last year\u2019s regime change was expected to help sever links between politicians and cops, but there has been no discernable change. A case in point is the appointment of a retired police officer who actively took part in the NPP\u2019s election campaigns as the CID Director."
  },
