    "md5": "55d803ff73061ddc4450acc17505b34a",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1299,
    "chunk_text": "One cannot but agree with the new police chief. It however needs to be added that the sorry state of affairs in the Police Department is also due to the subservience of some of its officers and men to politicians. Last year\u2019s regime change was expected to help sever links between politicians and cops, but there has been no discernable change. A case in point is the appointment of a retired police officer who actively took part in the NPP\u2019s election campaigns as the CID Director.\n\nInterestingly, former Chairman of the Election Commission Mahinda Deshapriya said yesterday at a ceremony to felicitate him that the practice of \u2018switching ballot boxes\u2019 had ended in 1981. However, large-scale election malpractices did not come to an end in that year. The outcomes of the presidential election and the referendum in 1982, and the elections in the late 1980s\u2014Provincial Council, Presidential and Parliamentary\u2014would have been different if they had been free and fair. We witnessed a similar situation in 1999 during the North Western Provincial council election, where the goon squads of the SLFP-led People\u2019s Alliance government, under President Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga\u2019s watch, chased away polling agents and stuffed the ballot boxes while the police were looking away."
