    "chunk_size_bytes": 1910,
    "chunk_text": "Interestingly, former Chairman of the Election Commission Mahinda Deshapriya said yesterday at a ceremony to felicitate him that the practice of \u2018switching ballot boxes\u2019 had ended in 1981. However, large-scale election malpractices did not come to an end in that year. The outcomes of the presidential election and the referendum in 1982, and the elections in the late 1980s\u2014Provincial Council, Presidential and Parliamentary\u2014would have been different if they had been free and fair. We witnessed a similar situation in 1999 during the North Western Provincial council election, where the goon squads of the SLFP-led People\u2019s Alliance government, under President Chandrika Bandaranaike Kumaratunga\u2019s watch, chased away polling agents and stuffed the ballot boxes while the police were looking away.\n\nThere are no paragons of virtue in Sri Lankan politics. The governments led by the UNP and the SLFP used underworld characters to perpetrate crimes such as assassinations and attacks on democracy, but the JVP itself committed many crimes and they included countless murders, incidents of assault, armed robberies and arson attacks on state-owned properties. All these political parties and their breakaway groups do not seem to feel any remorse for their past crimes.\n\nIGP Weerasooriya has rightly prioritised the task of ridding the police of lawbreakers. In fact, a considerable number of bad cops have already been sacked and prosecuted. The police deserve praise for that. However, the success of the new Police Chief\u2019s efforts to cleanse and revitalise the police hinges on his ability to depoliticise his department, which is full of servile elements ready to lick politicians\u2019 boots or sandals.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
