    "md5": "96895dc665506cd1a7c97be5ed9a7bd9",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1502,
    "chunk_text": "Satellite Fiasco: Fish or cut bait!\n\nThe NPP government has been concocting various theories to save face since the backfiring of its propaganda claim that the Mahinda Rajapaksa government invested state funds to the tune of USD 320 million in a failed satellite project. Prime Minister Dr. Harini Amarasuirya\u2019s recent statement in Parliament that no such investment had been made, but some financial benefits had accrued from the project to Sri Lanka has exasperated the JVP members of the NPP government beyond measure. They insist that the statement the PM made in answer to a question raised by an Opposition MP was based on incorrect information provided by some Board of Investment (BoI) officials. Curiously, they have not denied the fact that no state funds were invested in the satellite project.\n\nThe SLPP is trying to use the PM\u2019s statement in question to dupe the public into believing that all other allegations the NPP has made against the former government leaders are equally false. This is an instance of false generalisation. Those allegations should be investigated separately. The SLPP, which became a metaphor for corruption, cannot pull the wool over the eyes of the public with the help of such logical fallacies.\n\nThe government should stop trying to obfuscate the satellite issue. It should either admit that it made a mistake by claiming that state funds had been invested in the satellite project or prove that the PM was misled by some officials and their claim is true."
  },
