    "md5": "842b82cbde3d027aa055b7782e4438fc",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1226,
    "chunk_text": "The government should stop trying to obfuscate the satellite issue. It should either admit that it made a mistake by claiming that state funds had been invested in the satellite project or prove that the PM was misled by some officials and their claim is true.\n\nLet the government be urged to have the BoI officials concerned summoned to Parliament and questioned without further delay. After all, it had IGP Deshabandu Tennakoon sacked with the help of Parliament the other day. If the BoI officials are summoned, they will be able to tell their side of the story. Public officials affected by allegations that politicians make in Parliament have no way of defending themselves. This is a grave injustice. The NPP politicians ought to abandon the practice of making unsubstantiated allegations against public officials. They should also stop whining like the Opposition and take steps to prove its claim that state funds were invested in the satellite project and the country suffered a loss as a result. It should fish or cut bait.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
