    "md5": "103d53fe0eb2a9db51dac73d10f107b7",
    "chunk_size_bytes": 1887,
    "chunk_text": "Interest in Combank stocks enlivens CSE as ASPI crosses 20,000 points for the first time\n\nThe CSE started on a dull note but subsequently brightened up, mostly pushed by interest in banking stocks, especially by a Commercial Bank post interim results announcement yesterday.\n\nAmid those developments, the All Share Price Index crossed 20,000 points for the first time in history.\n\nProvisional data showed the ASPI was up 1.65 percent, or 328.68 points, at 20,257.35, while the S&P SL20 was up 2.14 percent, or 123.68 points, at 5,904.26.\n\nMarket turnover was Rs 9.5 billion with fourteen crossings. Top six crossings were reported in LOLC 252,000 shares, crossed to the tune of Rs 142 million; its shares traded at Rs 550, Sampath Bank 850,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 119 million; its shares traded at Rs 140,CT Holdings 150,000 shares crossed for Rs 105 million; its shares traded at Rs 700, Singer (SriLanka) 105 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 104 million; its shares traded at Rs 69, HNB 170,000 shares crossed for Rs 64 million; JKH 2.5 million shares crossed for Rs 57.5 million; its shares traded at Rs 23.\n\nIn the retail market companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; Sierra Cables Rs 659 million (36 million shares traded), HNB Rs 545 million (1.4 million shares traded), Access Engineering Rs 479 million (8.2 million shares traded), Commercial Bank Rs 371 million (2.1 million shares traded), LOLC Rs 328 million (586,000 shares traded), Lanka Venture Engineering Finance Rs 324 million (34 million shares traded) and JKH Rs 254 million (11 million shares traded). During the day 333 million share volumes changed hands in 51764 transactions.\n\nTop contributors to the ASPI were; Commercial Bank up Rs 8.75 at 181.25, DFCC Bank up Rs 7 at 160.25, LOLC Holdings up Rs 29.25 at 581, NTB up Rs 18.75 at 265, and Sampath Bank up Rs 2.25 at 142.50."
