    "chunk_text": "In the retail market companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; Sierra Cables Rs 659 million (36 million shares traded), HNB Rs 545 million (1.4 million shares traded), Access Engineering Rs 479 million (8.2 million shares traded), Commercial Bank Rs 371 million (2.1 million shares traded), LOLC Rs 328 million (586,000 shares traded), Lanka Venture Engineering Finance Rs 324 million (34 million shares traded) and JKH Rs 254 million (11 million shares traded). During the day 333 million share volumes changed hands in 51764 transactions.\n\nTop contributors to the ASPI were; Commercial Bank up Rs 8.75 at 181.25, DFCC Bank up Rs 7 at 160.25, LOLC Holdings up Rs 29.25 at 581, NTB up Rs 18.75 at 265, and Sampath Bank up Rs 2.25 at 142.50.\n\nProfits at Commercial Bank grew 101 percent from a year ago to Rs 15.9 billion in the June 2025 quarter helped by a reduction in loan loss provisions and net interest income growth.\n\nProfits at NDB Bank fell 6 percent from a year ago to Rs 2,447 million in the June 2025 quarter, amid net interest income and fee growth and a decline in fair value gains.\n\nSampath Bank profits fell 17 percent in the June 2025 quarter to Rs 6.7 billion, due to higher operating expenses.\n\nProfits at NTB grew 11 percent from a year ago to Rs 4.7 billion helped by higher net interest income, and lower provisions.\n\nProfits at HNB, which also has an insurance unit, grew 37 percent from a year ago to Rs 11.74 billion, helped by loan loss reversals and depreciation gains, despite a fall in net interest income.\n\nThe rupee opened at Rs 301.25/35 to the US dollar in the spot market yesterday, weaker from Rs 301.05/25 the previous day, while bond yields were broadly steady except for the 2033 tenor, which was down, dealers said.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2028 was quoted at 8.85/95 percent, down from 8.88/97 percent.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2029 was quoted flat at 9.38/42 percent."
