    "chunk_text": "The housing bubble proper was fired by macro-economists largely with the use of a scarce reserve regime in a floating exchange rate in the Fed, over a period of about 7 years after making claims that there was \u2018deflation\u2019 in the late 1990s.\n\nThe International Monetary Fund has also given technical assistance to operate a single policy rate with state liquidity forecasts instead of a scarce reserve regime after giving technical assistance earlier to calculate potential output. (Colombo/Aug18/2025)"
