    "chunk_text": "\u201cFree education,\u201d\u00a0in its truest sense, is a far more radical and empowering concept. It is not about the absence of cost but the presence of choice and opportunity. It is a system that aims to liberate the individual, to provide them with the tools and the freedom to pursue their aspirations, regardless of their socioeconomic background. In a true \u201cfree education\u201d system, the state\u2019s role shifts from that of a monolithic provider to that of a facilitator and an enabler. Its primary responsibility is to ensure equity\u2014to guarantee that every child, particularly those from poor and marginalised communities, has access to high-quality educational opportunities. This does not necessarily mean that the state must own and operate every school and university. Instead, it can be achieved through a variety of mechanisms, such as targeted scholarships, voucher systems, and public-private partnerships. The goal is to create a diverse and dynamic educational landscape where individuals have the freedom to choose the learning path that best suits their talents and ambitions.\n\nLeave a Reply Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment * Name *\n\nSave my name, email, and website in this browser for the next time I comment."
