    "chunk_text": "Invigorated performance by stock market continues; turnover tops Rs 11 billion\n\nThe CSE was extremely bullish but stabilized yesterday after surpassing the psychological barrier of 20,000 Index points the previous day, market analysts said.\n\nAmid those developments both indices moved upwards. The All Share Price Index went up by 165.7 points while S and P SL20 rose by 68.46 points. Turnover stood at Rs 11.1 billion with 12 crossings. Of the12 crossings the top seven crossings were reported in HNB, which crossed four million shares to the tune of Rs 1.6 billion; its shares traded at 405.50, HNB Finance 107 million shares crossed to the tune of Rs 851 million; its shares traded at Rs 7.90.\n\nHNB (Non-Voting) 2.2 million shares crossed for Rs 715 million; its shares traded at Rs 317,Commercial Bank (Voting) 500,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 99.2 million; its shares traded at Rs 199, Lanka IOC 700,000 shares crossed for Rs 92.4 million; its shares traded at Rs 32, Dialog Axiata 3.4 million shares crossed for Rs 76.2 million; its shares sold at Rs 22 and Digital Mobility Solutions 400,000 shares crossed to the tune of Rs 47.2 million; its shares fetched Rs 118.\n\nIn the retail market top companies that mainly contributed to the turnover were; HNB Finance Rs 475 million (53.8 million shares traded), LBL Energy Fund Rs 459 million (45 million shares traded), Sierra Cables Rs 314 million (15.5 million shares traded), Sampath Bank Rs 290 million (1.9 million shares traded), HNB Rs 261 million (641,000 shares traded), Commercial Bank Rs 195 million (991,000 shares traded) and JKH Rs 189 million (8 million shares traded). During the day 454 million share volumes changed hands in 52000 transactions.\n\nYesterday the rupee opened at Rs 301.60/75 to the US dollar in the spot market, weaker from Rs 301.55/70 the previous day, while bond yields edged up on the medium tenors, dealers said.\n\nA bond maturing on 15.12.2026 was quoted flat at 8.05/15 percent."
